From 66481d4a5c61d4ad478c67a9d7063be7df448eb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 07:31:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 107/112] Drive LPF: bass compensation, and real 2x
 oversampling with polyphase IIR half-band filters

Bass: 1.2.1's drive ladder lost its bass with resonance (40 Hz at -45 dBFS: -3 to -14 dB; small signals -13 dB at
half resonance), and by how much depended on the level, as its feedback tanh limits at about -54 dBFS. The input now
gets x (1 + k G^4) + 2 k T(c x), the loop's own DC terms (T its feedback tanh, c its feedback weights' sum), so y = x
is the loop's steady state at DC at every level: 40 Hz within 0.53 dB of resonance 0's (tests/filters drive_test),
while the loop itself (its self-oscillation, level and saturation) is as before. Without resonance nothing changes.

Oversampling: 1.2.1 ran the ladder twice on the same input and kept the second output (no filter), only above a
cutoff with resonance, and lowered the cutoff for it. Now the drive ladder runs at 88.2 kHz at every cutoff and
resonance (unless cpuDireness reaches 14, 1.2.1's guard; the switch is crossfaded), between a polyphase IIR half-band
interpolator and decimator (halfband.h: 5 allpass coefficients, HIIR's elliptic design; passband to 18 kHz within
0.0005 dB, images and aliases above 26.1 kHz at -88 dB; 2.3 samples of delay at 44.1 kHz, which lines up with the
dry fade, the parallel route and a crossfade's copy where a 55-tap FIR's 13.5 would have to be delayed in each), its
tanhs at the double rate. Aliasing of a 5..17 kHz tone 4.5..22 dB lower (hard clipping's slowly falling harmonics
still fold at 2x). The self-oscillation's pitch closer to the cutoff (-7 / -30 cents at 500 Hz / 2 kHz, was -16 / -56).
CPU (stereo, 128 frames): 75k instructions at 2x, 28k at 1x (was 20k; 37k where 1.2.1 oversampled).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
